{"name":"Dark Horizon","hex":"#666699","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dark","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having an absolute or (more often) relative lack of light.","Extinguished."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A complete or (more often) partial absence of light.","Ignorance."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dark"},{"term":"horizon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The visible horizontal line (in all directions) where the sky appears to meet the earth in the distance.","The range or limit of one's knowledge, experience or interest; a boundary or threshold."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/horizon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dark Horizon","blocks":[{"text":"Dark Horizon, released as Tarr Chronicles: Guardians of the Border in Russia, is a space combat simulation game developed by Russian team Quazar Studio and published by Paradox Interactive. The game released in North America on September 23, 2008. Dark Horizon is the prequel to Tarr Chronicles."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d6/Dark_Horizon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dark_Horizon","wikidata":"Q5223259"},{"title":"Horizon","blocks":[{"text":"Most commonly, the horizon is the border between the surface of a celestial body and its sky when viewed from the perspective of an observer on or above the surface of the celestial body. This concept is further refined as:"}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Horizons.svg/330px-Horizons.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Horizon","wikidata":"Q43261"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/d6/Dark_Horizon.jpg/250px-Dark_Horizon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia